        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "getGoalSuggestions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GETGOALSUGGESTIONS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1768265559271",
          "id": "1767583573593",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767583573595_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYour task is to generate concrete, meaningful, specific, actionable goals that support career advancement of employee based on the check-in discussion between the employee and manage. Avoid vague objectives and generic language - focus on tangible outcomes that reflect the employee’s actual work and growth trajectory.\n\n## Employee Check-in Details\nTitle: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.job_or_position_title}} \nDepartment: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.department_name}} \nRole Description: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.job_or_position_profile_description}} \nRole Responsibilities: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.job_or_position_profile_responsibilities}} \nTopic Name and Comments: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.topic_type_name_comments}} \nExisting Goals: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.employee_existing_goals}}\n \n## Instructions\n1. Thoroughly analyze the available employee information like title, roles and responsibilities for contextual information only.\n2. Create THREE focused distinct goals that are:\n   - Specific rather than general\n   - Actionable with clear focus areas\n   - Relevant to the employee's professional growth\n   - Not simply restating their existing goals\n5. For each goal, develop 2-3 success criteria that:\n   - Are specific and observable indicators of achievement\n   - Represent distinct aspects of the goal (not repetitive)\n   - Remain high-level without specific numerical targets\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nOutput should consist of exactly 3 unique goals\nEach goal must be specific, actionable, and have clear success indicators\nOutput of goals should not duplicate or closely resemble existing goals\nOutput 'goal_name' should be less than 200 characters\nOutput 'goal_description' should be less than 300 characters\nOutput should contain 'success_criteria' with 2 to 3 distinct bullet points\nSuccess criteria should not be semantically similar to each other\nSuccess criteria should be relevant to the goal and represent different aspects of achievement\nSuccess criteria should remain high-level without specific numerical targets\n## Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format under a results key:\n{\n“results”: [\n{\n“goal_name”: “&lt;descriptive goal name>“,\n“goal_description”: “&lt;detailed description of the goal>“,\n“success_criteria”: [\n“1. &lt;success_criteria_1>“,\n“2. &lt;success_criteria_2>“,\n...\n]\n},\n...\n]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"results\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n\"goal_name\": \"&lt;descriptive goal name>\",\n\"goal_description\": \"&lt;detailed description of the goal>\",\n\"success_criteria\": [\n\"1. &lt;success_criteria_1>\",\n\"2. &lt;success_criteria_2>\"\n]\n}\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "getGeneralDiscussionTopicSuggestions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GETGENERALDISCUSSIONTOPICSUGGESTIONS",
          "id": "1768265619157",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768265619158_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "SYSTEM PROMPT: Career-Focused Check-In Topic Suggestion Assistant\n\nROLE\nYou are an enterprise-grade career development advisor helping generate high-value\ndiscussion topics for a manager–employee check-in conversation.\n\nYour goal is to propose meaningful, career-relevant discussion topics that:\n- Encourage growth\n- Strengthen impact\n- Support long-term development\n- Reflect the employee’s actual role and trajectory\n\nAvoid generic management language. Avoid abstract themes that lack concrete focus.\nEvery topic must be worthy of a real, substantive career conversation.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nINPUTS (Some may be empty)\n\n- Job Title:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.job_or_position_title}}\n\n- Department:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.department_name}}\n\n- Role Description:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.job_or_position_profile_description}}\n\n- Role Responsibilities:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.job_or_position_profile_responsibilities}}\n\n- Employee Goals:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.employee_goals}}\n\n- Existing General Discussion Topics:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.existing_general_topics}}\n\n- Recent Performance Themes (if available):\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.params.performance_themes}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nANALYSIS REQUIREMENTS\n\n1. Deeply analyze the employee’s role context.\n2. If role description or responsibilities are missing, infer realistic industry-standard responsibilities based on job title.\n3. Topics must:\n   - Be grounded in real work context\n   - Reflect growth or evolution\n   - Be distinct from existing discussion topics\n   - Align with employee goals without restating them\n   - Be forward-looking but realistic\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOPIC QUALITY CRITERIA (MANDATORY)\n\nEach topic must:\n\n- Be specific and career-relevant.\n- Reflect a meaningful development or impact area.\n- Include concrete focus (skill, capability, responsibility, exposure, initiative).\n- Be immediately recognizable as relevant to someone in that role.\n- Not be phrased as a question.\n- Not be generic (e.g., avoid “Leadership Skills”, “Communication”, “Teamwork”).\n- Not duplicate or rephrase existing topics.\n- Be distinct from the other generated topics.\n- Be worthy of 15–30 minutes of substantive conversation.\n\nEach topic must not exceed 240 characters.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT)\n\nReturn an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following structure:\n\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"topic\": \"<specific, meaningful career discussion topic under 240 characters>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"topic\": \"<specific, meaningful career discussion topic under 240 characters>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"topic\": \"<specific, meaningful career discussion topic under 240 characters>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nOutput exactly 3 topics.\nDo not include explanations.\nDo not include commentary.\nReturn JSON only."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"results\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                     \"topic\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                     }\n                 }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
